Then you'll just have to accept my conversations with hundreds of people
on freenode's #nethack (and other) channels over the past couple of years, 
almost all of whom listed Sokoban both as a thing they need to do (because 
of the rings, wands, and 50% potential for reflection) and also a thing 
that takes a lot of relatively boring time.  So while "anyone" may 
be slightly too sweeping, I still consider the vast majority of Nethack 
players to only find Sokoban amusing while it's still relatively new to 
them.  And I even have plenty of "excuse" to do so.  (I also listen to 
all the people who clamor for new Sokoban levels because they're bored 
with the old ones, as well as the oft-committed YANI to "just make a 
random Soko generator.")  

Again, quibbling over semantics doesn't help solve the problem, it just 
generates more dribble on RGRN, instead of actual discussion.  If you
want to be productive instead of a nuisance, then let's talk about what
(if anything) should be done with Sokoban, shall we?  I've already pointed 
out what I see as problems, (as have some other people), but let me sum 
up again for you:

1. It's too unlike the rest of Nethack
2. It's too invariant; once you memorize it, much of the appeal vanishes
3. The prize reward is potentially too great for the effort required

Fixing 1. directly by changing Soko completely to something else annoys
the purists and the people who actually like Soko and just were tired of
the same old levels over and over.  Not productive.

Fixing 2. directly by generating a randomized Soko runs a heavy risk 
of annoying the crap out of the people who do NOT find playing Sokoban 
fun, and who wanted to play a roguelike instead.

Fixing 3. directly is also dangerous; if you reduce the reward too
significantly, then you just have people skipping the last level and
never finishing the puzzle; if you remove the rings and wands, people
may never bother doing it in the first place unless they need food.  If
you're going to do THAT, why even have the branch at all?  Leaving it 
unchanged would be a better option at that point.

That's where I've been for about six months now.  I don't like the
current Soko; I think most people tolerate it because they get good loot
out of it.  But I haven't seen anything worthwhile to replace it with,
and leaving it alone in the meantime is much better; cf. "the devil you
know" and all that.

